  "title": "Calculating Ka and Kb from pH (CyberLearn)",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "strong": true,
                "text": "Change examples and activities to majority/minority reasoning?"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0fxtp0aekrmbcxj",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "On this page, we will look at examples of calculating "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "b"
              },
              {
                "text": " values given pH."
              }
            ],
            "id": "no681umgq3jwraj",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1749132606",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pH of a 0.0516-M solution of nitrous acid, HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is 2.34. What is its "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "iqn8k5zr0y82ksd",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "mh7ssbgucd9cfab",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "plfvl96sodbla5b",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm{HNO}}_2(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{NO}}_2^-(aq)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "z1c7w2k9jxoenhx",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "Determine [H"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "n0nfmjunrc6nfe2",
                        "strong": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "3"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "08p1xxb3d8r2u24",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "zbfnc37rj5ohemy",
                        "strong": true,
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "d8v4lifgsuspgit",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "] from pH."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "03v1udfwyzlivcu",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "0ha3cqrgq0nef53",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To get the various values in the ICE (Initial, Change, Equilibrium) table, we first calculate [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "], the equilibrium concentration of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", from the pH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "db140wd1s3wkplj",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "la1zhdh4wb6pfox",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8cw4gju4n5nq463",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\;=\\;10^{-2.34}\\;=\\;0.0046\\mathrm M",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "zinzlh4kasqtiin",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "Fill the ICE chart based on the inial concentration of HA and the calculated equilibrium concentration of H"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "tq1wfgm3nw97dq8",
                        "strong": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "3"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "8srh6yqp6j72s3d",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "nrti2fbm03879e8",
                        "strong": true,
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "r6dvv9i9ugmar8m",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "ety1gew2270adeu",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wji5sebbjpz0v6v",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The change in concentration of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "[H"
                  },
                  {
                    "doublesub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is the difference between the equilibrium concentration of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which we determined from the pH, and the initial concentration, [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "i"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". The initial concentration of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is its concentration in pure water, which is so much less than the final concentration that we approximate it as zero (~0)."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "x9iux8xek0cua99",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The change in concentration of NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is equal to the change in concentration of [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]. For each 1 mol of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that forms, 1 mol of NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " forms. The equilibrium concentration of HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is equal to its initial concentration plus the change in its concentration."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "c3iggymlob2s6bc",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Now we can fill in the ICE table with the concentrations at equilibrium, as shown here:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a5hhatga5vfzyh4",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "___selfClosing___": true,
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "id": "hqea51rl43fvure",
                            "text": " ",
                            "type": "text"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "9iu3gvovzr2kwgz",
                        "type": "td"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "id": "xy6sbu8tb9e8icc",
                            "text": "          HNO"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "bnft7bedhxvbhh9",
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "2"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "uuvk1nolxonob7a",
                            "text": "             +            H"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "hfyh1qxty41s28h",
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "2"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "i5xb7rdwh4cy91s",
